{"title":"CraneParcel","sub":"One parcel in eight needs a second trip","type":"Cost & operations","industry":"Parcel delivery","geo":"United States","diff":1,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Last-mile economics · option comparison","prompt":"CraneParcel delivers 30 million parcels a year for online retailers in the Northeast. About 12% of first delivery attempts fail because nobody is home, and each redelivery costs about $6. The operations director has two ideas: text customers a one-hour delivery window, or install parcel lockers. Which should come first?","clarify":[{"q":"Delivery windows?","a":"Customers get a text with a one-hour window and can redirect the parcel. In a trial, failures fell to 7%. Texts and tracking cost about $0.05 a parcel."},{"q":"Lockers?","a":"1,500 lockers at $8k each to install and $1.2k a year to run. About 8% of parcels would go to lockers. Only 1% of locker deliveries fail, and dropping many parcels at one locker saves about $1.20 a parcel."},{"q":"Can both be done?","a":"Yes; budget is the constraint this year."}],"structure":{"root":"How should CraneParcel cut failed deliveries?","branches":[{"head":"Size of the problem","items":["Failures × redelivery cost"]},{"head":"Delivery windows","items":["Failures avoided","Cost per parcel"]},{"head":"Lockers","items":["Failures avoided","Cheaper drops","Investment"]}]},"hypothesis":"Windows apply to every parcel at almost no cost, so they probably save the most quickly. Lockers need investment and only reach a small share of parcels.","questions":[{"q":"How much do failed deliveries cost today?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>30M × 12% = 3.6M redeliveries × $6 = <b>$21.6M a year</b>.</p>"},{"q":"Compare the two ideas.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"388.46pt\" height=\"159.66pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 388.46 159.66\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 159.66 L 388.46 159.66 L 388.46 -0 L 0 -0 L 0 159.66 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 35.3 133.76 L 381.26 133.76 L 381.26 11.792 L 35.3 11.792 L 35.3 133.76 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"ma99844d2ee\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#ma99844d2ee\" x=\"120.916364\" y=\"133.76\" style=\"fill: #4a5568; stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(85.541442 149.985) scale(0.09 -0.09)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-21\" d=\"M 595 0 L 595 4467 L 2093 4467 Q 2650 4467 3062 4220 Q 3475 3974 3699 3478 Q 3923 2982 3923 2234 Q 3923 1485 3699 989 Q 3475 493 3062 246 Q 2650 0 2093 0 L 595 0 z\nM 1133 474 L 2093 474 Q 2464 474 2745 640 Q 3027 806 3187 1116 Q 3347 1427 3347 1869 L 3347 2598 Q 3347 3040 3187 3353 Q 3027 3667 2745 3830 Q 2464 3994 2093 3994 L 1133 3994 L 1133 474 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-6\" d=\"M 1786 -77 Q 1338 -77 1005 137 Q 672 352 486 739 Q 301 1126 301 1651 Q 301 2176 486 2563 Q 672 2950 1005 3164 Q 1338 3379 1786 3379 Q 2227 3379 2547 3171 Q 2867 2963 3040 2598 Q 3213 2234 3213 1766 L 3213 1523 L 838 1523 L 838 1370 Q 838 941 1097 656 Q 1357 371 1818 371 Q 2131 371 2364 518 Q 2598 666 2726 941 L 3091 678 Q 2931 346 2592 134 Q 2253 -77 1786 -77 z\nM 1786 2950 Q 1510 2950 1296 2822 Q 1082 2694 960 2467 Q 838 2240 838 1952 L 838 1907 L 2662 1907 L 2662 1978 Q 2662 2272 2553 2489 Q 2445 2707 2246 2828 Q 2048 2950 1786 2950 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-f\" d=\"M 1542 0 L 1088 0 Q 826 0 685 150 Q 544 301 544 531 L 544 4736 L 1056 4736 L 1056 448 L 1542 448 L 1542 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-