 Q 1542 2643 1805 2586 L 2150 2509 Q 2611 2406 2899 2246 Q 3187 2086 3318 1852 Q 3450 1619 3450 1280 Q 3450 883 3254 592 Q 3059 301 2716 144 Q 2374 -13 1926 -13 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-2a\" d=\"M 595 0 L 595 4467 L 1312 4467 L 2157 2886 L 2592 2061 L 2624 2061 L 3066 2886 L 3910 4467 L 4602 4467 L 4602 0 L 4077 0 L 4077 3014 L 4077 3763 L 4045 3763 L 3667 3014 L 2598 1069 L 1530 3014 L 1152 3763 L 1120 3763 L 1120 3014 L 1120 0 L 595 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-ae\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-2a\" transform=\"translate(59.796875 0)\"/></g></g></g><g id=\"patch_3\"><path d=\"M 51.025455 133.76 L 190.807273 133.76 L 190.807273 17.6 L 51.025455 17.6 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pb0c4f41920)\" style=\"fill: #c2410c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_4\"><path d=\"M 225.752727 133.76 L 365.534545 133.76 L 365.534545 91.9424 L 225.752727 91.9424 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pb0c4f41920)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_5\"><path d=\"M 35.3 133.76 L 35.3 11.792 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 35.3 133.76 L 381.26 133.76 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_8\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(115.028239 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\" d=\"M 1696 0 L 1120 0 L 2829 4006 L 922 4006 L 922 3174 L 442 3174 L 442 4467 L 3373 4467 L 3373 3994 L 1696 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" d=\"M 870 -77 Q 672 -77 576 28 Q 480 134 480 294 L 480 378 Q 480 544 576 646 Q 672 749 870 749 Q 1075 749 1168 646 Q 1261 544 1261 378 L 1261 294 Q 1261 134 1168 28 Q 1075 -77 870 -77 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" d=\"M 3187 4467 L 3187 3994 L 1229 3994 L 1101 2291 L 1146 2291 Q 1254 2445 1376 2553 Q 1498 2662 1664 2723 Q 1830 2784 2061 2784 Q 2445 2784 2745 2617 Q 3046 2451 3219 2144 Q 3392 1837 3392 1402 Q 3392 966 3213 633 Q 3034 301 2698 112 Q 2362 -77 1888 -77 Q 1517 -77 1254 35 Q 992 147 809 320 Q 627 493 493 685 L 896 992 Q 1069 730 1277 566 Q 1485 403 1888 403 Q 2342 403 2582 646 Q 2822 890 2822 1331 L 2822 1395 Q 2822 1837 2582 2080 Q 2342 2323 1888 2323 Q 1581 2323 1405 2211 Q 1229 2099 1088 1946 L 634 2010 L 794 4467 L 3187 4467 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_9\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(289.755511 89.7424) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pb0c4f41920\"><rect x=\"35.3\" y=\"11.792\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Yearly saving ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p><b>Windows:</b> failures fall 5 points: 30M × 5% × $6 = $9.0M, less 30M × $0.05 = $1.5M: <b>$7.5M a year</b>, no investment.</p> <p><b>Lockers:</b> 8% of parcels = 2.4M; each avoids 11 points of failures (× $6 = $0.66) and saves $1.20 = $1.86 per parcel: $4.46M, less $1.8M running: <b>$2.7M a year</b>, for $12M upfront (payback 4.5 years).</p>"},{"q":"What would you do?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Launch delivery windows across the network now: bigger saving, no investment. Then add lockers in dense areas with the highest failure rates (apartment blocks, offices), where they fill fastest and pay back soonest.</p> <p>Careful: the two savings overlap. Once windows have cut failures to 7%, each locker parcel avoids only 6 points of failure, not 11: 2.4M × (6% × $6 + $1.20) − $1.8M ≈ <b>$1.9M a year</b>, a payback of about 6 years. So put lockers only where failure rates stay high after windows.</p>"}],"reco":"Start with one-hour delivery windows: they cut failures from 12% to about 7% across all 30 million parcels and save about $7.5M a year with no investment. Then roll out lockers in the densest, highest-failure areas: once windows are live, 1,500 lockers would save about $1.9M a year (about $2.7M on their own) for $12M upfront, paying back in about 6 years, so put them first where failures stay highest. Risk: customers ignoring texts. Next step: switch on windows region by region and track failures weekly.","great":["Sizes the problem first","Compares savings and investment for each option","Prioritises the option that reaches every parcel","Targets lockers where they pay back fastest"],"id":87,"slug":"craneparcel"}